{#
  templates/loki-openbao-audit-rule.yml.j2 — Loki RULER alerting-rule fragment
  SVC-07 contributes TO the shared SVC-18 (Loki) observability stack.

  Rendered by task 10.2 (tasks/alerts.yml, §10.2) into the Loki ruler's
  rule directory ({{ openbao_loki_audit_rule_file }}) that the SVC-18 Loki
  ruler component evaluates. This is a LogQL-derived alerting rule — the
  OpenBaoAuditFailure alert (Req 10.7) fires on a LOG SIGNAL (an audit-device
  write failure line), NOT on a Prometheus metric, so it lives here rather than
  in the Prometheus rule file (prometheus-openbao-alerts.yml.j2).

  WHY A LOKI RULE (not Prometheus): when OpenBao's file audit device fails to
  write, OpenBao fails CLOSED — it BLOCKS the triggering operation and returns
  an audit-distinct error (design.md Error Handling; Req 7.3 / FD.3). That
  failure surfaces as an ERROR line in OpenBao's OPERATIONAL log stream (stdout,
  JSON, shipped to Loki tagged service=openbao — task 5.x logging + the
  Promtail wiring in task 7.2). There is no clean Prometheus counter for "the
  audit sink is unwritable"; the log line is the authoritative signal. This rule
  matches that line and fires OpenBaoAuditFailure within 1 minute of the line's
  ingestion (Req 10.7).

  DISTINCT FROM THE SNAPSHOT ALERT: the nightly Raft snapshot failure emits its
  OWN marker (OPENBAO_SNAPSHOT_FAILURE, openbao_install: openbao_backup_failure_
  marker) and is a DIFFERENT alert with a 15-min window (task 11.1 / Req 11.2).
  This rule deliberately matches the AUDIT-WRITE-FAILURE signal only, via the
  openbao_audit_failure_log_matcher literal, so the two never conflate.

  AUTO-RESOLVE / one-shot nature: an audit-write failure is a fail-closed safety
  event — the rule fires as soon as a matching line is ingested within the short
  evaluation window; it clears when no further matching lines arrive in the
  window (Loki ruler resolves the alert when the query returns empty). The `for`
  is intentionally 0s so the FIRST matching line alerts inside the 1-min SLA.

  NO secret value is templated here — the LogQL matcher, labels, and window are
  all non-secret config. The audit LOG CONTENT itself (which may reference secret
  paths) is never inlined into this rule; the rule matches only the error-signal
  substring, not any secret material.
#}
# MANAGED BY ANSIBLE (openbao_init_unseal / task 10.2) — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
# Loki ruler alerting rule contributed by SVC-07 (OpenBao) to SVC-18.
# OpenBaoAuditFailure (critical): fires within 1 min of an audit-write-failure
# log line ingested from the OpenBao operational log stream (Req 10.7).
groups:
  - name: "{{ openbao_loki_audit_rule_group_name }}"
    # Evaluate frequently enough that the first matching line alerts well within
    # the 1-minute SLA (Req 10.7). Kept below the 1-min budget.
    interval: "{{ openbao_loki_audit_rule_interval }}"
    rules:
      - alert: OpenBaoAuditFailure
        # LogQL: count audit-write-failure lines in the OpenBao operational log
        # stream over a short window; fire when at least one is seen. The
        # matcher is scoped to service=openbao (the operational stream) and to
        # the audit-write-failure signal substring — NOT the snapshot marker.
        expr: >-
          {{ openbao_loki_audit_failure_expr }}
        # 0s so the first ingested matching line fires immediately (within the
        # {{ openbao_loki_audit_rule_interval }} evaluation cadence), keeping the
        # end-to-end fire well inside the 1-minute SLA (Req 10.7).
        for: "{{ openbao_loki_audit_failure_for }}"
        labels:
          severity: critical
          service: openbao
          # Routing label the Alertmanager route fragment keys off (Req 10.9);
          # the Loki ruler forwards firing alerts to the same Alertmanager.
          receiver_team: "{{ openbao_alert_primary_team_label }}"
        annotations:
          summary: "OpenBao audit device write failure (fail-closed)"
          description: >-
            An audit-device write-failure log line was ingested from the OpenBao
            operational log stream. OpenBao fails CLOSED on audit-write failure:
            the triggering operation is BLOCKED and an audit-distinct error is
            returned (Req 7.3 / FD.3). Secret operations are being refused until
            the audit sink is writable again. Investigate the audit volume
            ({{ openbao_audit_dir }}) immediately.
          runbook_url: "{{ openbao_alert_runbook_base }}#openbaoauditfailure"
